      behind the MOE_PER_EXPERT_DISPATCH property, default off.
    - patches/0041: skip expert-constant processing at compile time under
      per-expert dispatch; measured inert on the fused offload route.
    - patches/0042: THE FIX for 0037's page fault on the Arc Pro B60. Under
      the hybrid prefill split the grouped-GEMM tables hold only the
      resident (token, k) pairs and the rest of tokens_per_expert_cpu stays
      -1, but the gather kernel was launched over token_num * max_topk
      work-groups; every one past the fill read input[-HIDDEN_SIZE], one
      row before the activation buffer -- unmapped on Xe2 (xe page fault,
      device coredump, CL_OUT_OF_RESOURCES), mapped by luck on Xe-HPG. The
      gather and the stages it sizes now run over the filled count, and a
      batch with no resident expert takes the per-expert path as before
      0037. Bisected and measured 2026-09-17: the 35B at --offload-ratio 99
      --moe-cpu-tier serves on the B60, 23.6 t/s decode (KV u8, f16).

