marfrit-openvino (2026.4.0~dev20260821+p16-1) bookworm trixie; urgency=medium

  * One more patch applied on top of +p15, same upstream commit (71640275),
    same smallest-sufficient-divergence numbering:
    - patches/0037: under a static half-partition every MoE layer's routed
      batch contains at least one non-resident expert, and the two
      grouped-GEMM callers (on_before_prefill, build_grouped_mask_otd) called
      try_acquire_simultaneous without a cpu_tier_misses destination -- so
      the first non-resident entry returned nullopt and the WHOLE layer fell
      back to exec_prefill_onednn's per-expert loop: ~5,520 kernel launches
      where the grouped path needs ~120, on all 40 layers
      (grouped_fallbacks=400 per process). The fix wires cpu_tier_misses into
      both callers; non-resident entries take a sentinel slot id (num_expert)
      that the mask-gen kernels already exclude and scatter_reduce's
      UINT_MAX skip already handles, and the host tier runs them after the
      grouped GEMM completes. New OTD perf counter: hybrid_prefill_layers
      (arcint DESIGN 7.0.2bx).
    - MEASURED: grouped_fallbacks 400 -> 0, decode 18.2 t/s against a gate of
      14.8, 3.4 identity and E2 pass. The campaign's prefill gate (tier ON
      within 25 % of tier OFF) is NOT met -- the host dispatch for the
      non-resident experts serialises through ~128 experts per layer and
      dominates prefill -- and static-partition-prefill stays open. This
      level ships because the coding defect is gone, not because the
      campaign closed.

